pipe()

MinGW ships _pipe(), not pipe(), so this fixture does not compile on Windows.
Making it compile would not help: this registers the pipe fds with the reactor,
and Windows select() is socket-only -- it cannot poll a pipe or file fd at all,
so the select-based backend (src/async/io_iocp.c) could never service them.
Skipping is the honest answer; switching to _pipe() would trade a clear build
error for a hang.

See docs/archive/windows-pipe-reactor-fixtures-do-not-build.md
